he  same intention analysis can be applied  to her relationship with food is this  for nourishment and satisfaction is this  an emotional choice or is it a means of  restriction or to satisfy ravenous  hunger so whether we're talking about  food or alcohol we can apply some of  those same intuitive approaches from a  place of self-care not self-control  since i cut back so much on alcohol i  decided i'm not gonna focus on my diet  because that's not what's important  right now like cutting out the alcohol  is so much more important so i've been  eating whatever i want whatever i want  i've been craving sugar like you have no  idea and it turns into sugar in your  body so when i cut out the alcohol you  know it's like 11 o'clock at night and  i'm like i want a reese's like i  want an ice cream bar and i let myself  have it because i'm like i'm not going  to deprive myself of that too you know  one step at a time i'm being realistic  okay fact check alcohol itself doesn't  convert into sugar in the body but it  does cause blood sugars to rise a little  bit more so obviously if the alcohol is  mixed with like a sugar sweetened drink  like soda or juice but then after the  liver processes the booze you actually  end up with very low blood sugar levels  and this is sometimes why we feel kind  of shaky and ravenous in the morning  after drinking good morning  my guess is that jaclyn's sugar craving  has more to do with her emotional eating  tendencies and kind of getting that  dopamine hit from sugar in the absence  of alcohol some may call an experience  like this like a transfer addiction  where one coping mechanism like sugar is  replaced for another like alcohol i  weighed myself today and i've lost three  and a half pounds in the last three  weeks and that's me eating so much junk  goes to show how much denial i was in  like the inflammation that was in my  blood work last year was so high and i  just didn't want to admit that it was  alcohol it was so much easier to change  my diet and get my ass on the treadmill  than it was to admit i have an alcohol  problem so there is a positive  correlation between weight gain and  alcohol intake and there are a few  explanations for why this is for one  alcohol is more energy dense than carbs  or protein and provides about seven  calories per gram and this of course  would be increased when mixed with  something like juice or soda etc two  alcohol intake can also disrupt sleep  quality which can then increase appetite  the next day three chronic alcohol  consumption can increase inflammation  and water retention and lastly alcohol  often leads to disinhibition so we often  end up eating more now i imagine it took  a long time to get to this breakthrough  so my hope for jacqueline is that she  continues to develop her sense of  self-awareness emotional support and  coping strategies for her anxiety so  that she can not only positively impact  a relationship with food and alcohol but  also manage any other future life  symptoms that are thrown her way so on  that note that is all that i have for  you guys today thank you again to let's  get checked for sponsoring if you like  this video be sure to give it a thumbs  up leave me a comment below on what  you'd like to see me review next  subscribe to the channel and i'll see  you next time on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

